1
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:13,110
A design student must draw a regular hexagon logo, with guide lines at 60, 30 and 45 degrees.

2
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:16,620
She may only use a ruler and compasses.

3
00:00:16,670 --> 00:00:19,300
Is a protractor needed, or not allowed?

4
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:22,550
Pause the video and choose.

5
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,490
A protractor is not allowed.

6
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:27,050
In a construction, you use compasses.

7
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:32,460
Circles make exact equal lengths, and equal lengths make exact angles.

8
00:00:32,510 --> 00:00:36,080
Remember: an angle bisector cuts an angle in half.

9
00:00:36,130 --> 00:00:41,980
A perpendicular bisector meets a line at 90 degrees, through its midpoint.

10
00:00:42,030 --> 00:00:43,040
Draw a line A B.

11
00:00:43,090 --> 00:00:47,450
Put the compasses on A, and draw an arc that crosses the line at C.

12
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:48,840
Keep the same radius.

13
00:00:48,890 --> 00:00:54,130
Put the compasses on C, and draw an arc that crosses the first arc at D.

14
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:56,920
A C, A D and C D are all the same length.

15
00:00:56,970 --> 00:01:02,100
Triangle A C D is equilateral, so angle D A C is exactly 60 degrees.

16
00:01:02,150 --> 00:01:02,810
Your turn.

17
00:01:02,860 --> 00:01:06,860
If you bisect the 60 degree angle, what angle do you get?

18
00:01:06,910 --> 00:01:10,180
Pause the video and try it.

19
00:01:10,230 --> 00:01:12,180
Half of 60 is 30 degrees.

20
00:01:12,230 --> 00:01:18,900
For 45 degrees, construct a right angle with a perpendicular, then bisect it.

21
00:01:18,950 --> 00:01:21,360
Always leave your construction arcs.

22
00:01:21,410 --> 00:01:23,410
They show your method.

23
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:25,920
For a regular hexagon, draw a circle.

24
00:01:25,970 --> 00:01:30,480
Keep the same radius, and step it round the circle, marking points.

25
00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:32,120
Join the points.

26
00:01:32,170 --> 00:01:35,490
For a square, draw two diameters at right angles.

27
00:01:35,540 --> 00:01:39,680
For an octagon, bisect the right angles between them.

28
00:01:39,730 --> 00:01:40,350
Your turn.

29
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:44,640
Stepping the radius round a circle, how many points do you mark?

30
00:01:44,690 --> 00:01:47,510
Pause and work it out.

31
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,150
6 points.

32
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:56,370
Each side of the hexagon is the same as the radius, because it makes 6 equilateral triangles at the centre.

33
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:57,840
Here is the method.

34
00:01:57,890 --> 00:02:02,580
Step 1: 60 degrees comes from an equilateral triangle.

35
00:02:02,630 --> 00:02:07,540
Step 2: 90 degrees comes from a perpendicular bisector.

36
00:02:07,590 --> 00:02:12,990
Step 3: bisect to halve an angle: 30, 45, 15 degrees.

37
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:17,120
Step 4: keep the radius fixed, and leave the arcs.

38
00:02:17,170 --> 00:02:22,930
To construct 120 degrees, construct 60 degrees on a straight line.

39
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:28,580
The angle on the other side is 180 minus 60, which is 120.

40
00:02:28,630 --> 00:02:34,580
To construct 15 degrees, bisect 60 to get 30, then bisect again.

41
00:02:34,630 --> 00:02:43,600
A hexagon drawn in a circle of radius 5 centimetres has sides of 5 centimetres, so its perimeter is 30 centimetres.

42
00:02:43,650 --> 00:02:45,550
Dan constructs 60 degrees.

43
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:47,610
Which line is wrong?

44
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:48,700
Line 2 is wrong.

45
00:02:48,750 --> 00:02:53,810
The radius must stay the same, so that the triangle is equilateral.

46
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:57,980
The arc from C must also have radius 4 centimetres.

47
00:02:58,030 --> 00:03:02,710
Architects and engineers used compass constructions for centuries.

48
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:07,140
Today, design software uses exactly the same geometry.

49
00:03:07,190 --> 00:03:08,460
One last question.

50
00:03:08,510 --> 00:03:11,900
What angle do you get if you bisect 45 degrees?

51
00:03:11,950 --> 00:03:15,280
Pause the video and answer.

52
00:03:15,330 --> 00:03:18,590
Half of 45 is 22.5 degrees.

53
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:23,640
To remember: 60 degrees comes from an equilateral triangle.

54
00:03:23,690 --> 00:03:28,960
30 and 45 degrees come from bisecting 60 and 90.

55
00:03:29,010 --> 00:03:32,650
For a hexagon, step the radius round a circle.

56
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:37,220
Squares and octagons come from perpendicular diameters.

57
00:03:37,270 --> 00:03:42,430
Great work! Now practise lesson 5.4 on Camday.
